{"findings":[{"rule_id":"TL-002","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D7","page":1,"quote":"⌀12"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D15","page":1,"quote":"⌀9"}],"comment":"The stepped shaft diameters (D7 ⌀12 and D15 ⌀9) carry no fit or tolerance callouts, leaving mating features to general tolerances. This risks improper assembly with mating parts. The designer should add appropriate fit designations or explicit tolerances to these functional diameters."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Add fit or tolerance callouts to dimensions D7 and D15."},{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"note","ref":"N1","page":1,"quote":"NOTE : (English) # MATERIAL: M.S. # FINISH: I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT) # MACHINING: 3.2 # WEIGHT(Kg ): 0.04 kg"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D7","page":1,"quote":"⌀12"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D15","page":1,"quote":"⌀9"}],"comment":"Note N1 specifies an I.Z.B.P. (trivalent zinc plating) finish, but the mating shaft diameters D7 (⌀12) and D15 (⌀9) have no allowance for plating thickness. Plating buildup on uncontrolled tight fits can cause interference during assembly. The designer should either specify pre-plate dimensions that account for coating thickness or add a note defining the plating thickness allowance.","recommended_correction":"Specify pre-plate dimensions or add plating thickness allowances for the coated mating features."}]}
